course: dictionary
lesson: 3298
title: Eternally: for ever, always, very
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eternally comes from eternal, which means lasting for ever, with no beginning and no end. In everyday talk, it often means always or very much. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to pick.
explain: In «where all waistcoat pockets are eternally situated», the pockets are not going anywhere. Situated means placed, so eternally must mean always, in that same place. The joke is that the pocket is always there, and yet it isn't.
explain: When someone says «I'll be eternally grateful», they do not mean they will be thankful for ever and ever. They mean they are very, very grateful. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit the sentence? If it does, you have found it.
fact: Eternally means for ever, or always, or very much, depending on the sentence.
fact: Eternal means lasting for ever, with no beginning or end.
fact: «Eternally late» means always late, very often late.
fact: «Eternally grateful» is a warm way to say very grateful.
fact: Check a new meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word.
exercise: Struggling with his gown, he reaches «where all waistcoat pockets are eternally situated». What does eternally mean here? | Behind the waistcoat | *Always, in the same place | Sometimes, now and then | Very quickly
exercise: Ella says, «I'll be eternally grateful for your help.» What does eternally mean here? | *Very, very grateful | Grateful only until lunchtime | Not grateful at all | Grateful for one day
exercise: Tom is «eternally late» for school. What does eternally mean here? | Once in a blue moon | Lost in a maze | *Always, very often | Early every day
test: «Her cheerful grin was eternally fixed on her face.» What does eternally mean here? | Painfully | *Always | Quickly | Rarely
test: Christians believe in eternal life. What does eternal mean? | Very cheap | Happening once a year | *Lasting for ever, with no end | Lasting one week
exam: Which word best replaces eternally in «I'll be eternally grateful»? | Quietly | *Greatly | Lazily | Hungrily
